  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Single-GPU evaluation only: although the host server has 8x A800 GPUs, all reported evaluation metrics run on 1 GPU; multi-GPU tensor-parallel NCCL coordination and cross-card wake-ups are not empirically measured.",
    "Trusted-engine / single-tenant assumption (§5): sharing a CUDA Primary Context removes hardware driver-level process isolation; sharing contexts across untrusted multi-tenant workloads is explicitly out of scope.",
    "Single active engine per GPU (§2): multiple sleeping engines may reside on a GPU, but at most one engine wakes up and executes at a time; concurrent spatial GPU sharing is outside scope.",
    "No CUDA Graphs support (§5): checkpointing/restoring CUDA graphs requires preserving or rewriting embedded device pointers and kernel references and is left to future work.",
    "Engine & workload coverage: implementation and benchmarks cover vLLM v0.19.1 only (SGLang is not benchmarked); 59-99% kernel similarity relies on shared operators/libraries (e.g., FlashInfer, cuBLAS), and host DRAM (1 TB in testbed) must store weights, host CPU contexts, and checkpointed GPU buffers.",
    "Cold-start and PhoenixOS weight-loading times in Fig. 7 (right) are normalized to remove storage I/O overhead."
  ],
